00:01:51.082 --> 00:01:51.948
Hello?


00:01:52.849 --> 00:01:53.750
Is anybody home?


00:01:54.884 --> 00:01:56.554
- Hi!
- Hi there.


00:01:57.088 --> 00:01:59.656
- My name's Karen. What's yours?
- Ashley.


00:02:00.558 --> 00:02:02.126
What did I tell you
about talking to strangers?


00:02:02.893 --> 00:02:04.794
She's not a stranger.
She's Karen.


00:02:05.728 --> 00:02:07.029
Dr. Karen Cavanaugh.


00:02:07.031 --> 00:02:09.033
I'm the researcher
from Eastern State.


00:02:22.480 --> 00:02:23.481
Oh, my God.


00:02:24.782 --> 00:02:25.950
Yeah,
it's a damn shame.


00:02:26.617 --> 00:02:28.050
Trying to off-load the meat,
you know?


00:02:28.052 --> 00:02:29.453
Make up for what
I lost in wool, but...


00:02:30.387 --> 00:02:31.822
who's gonna buy poisoned sheep?


00:02:43.200 --> 00:02:45.703
What does this one do?
And what about this one?


00:02:45.970 --> 00:02:47.705
Ashley,
leave Dr. Cavanaugh alone.


00:02:48.005 --> 00:02:50.241
It's okay. I could use
a research assistant.


00:02:50.774 --> 00:02:51.775
And what about this one?


00:02:52.910 --> 00:02:55.512
That analyzes soil samples
to see if there's anything


00:02:55.514 --> 00:02:57.315
in the ground that might be
poisoning the animals.


00:02:58.249 --> 00:02:59.216
And this one.


00:03:00.784 --> 00:03:03.018
That checks for pesticides
or any other poisons


00:03:03.020 --> 00:03:05.189
that might be
sprayed on the crops.


00:03:05.524 --> 00:03:07.791
And this is just a camera
for taking photos.


00:03:14.064 --> 00:03:14.899
Ashley?


00:03:16.401 --> 00:03:17.235
Ashley!


00:03:18.002 --> 00:03:19.935
Ashley?
What happened?


00:03:19.937 --> 00:03:22.039
I don't know. I looked up
and she was down.


00:03:23.108 --> 00:03:24.742
- Ash.
- She's barely breathing.


00:03:30.148 --> 00:03:31.648
I don't have a signal!


00:03:31.650 --> 00:03:34.150
Dr. Rowe's office is
just off Main Street. Come on.


00:03:34.152 --> 00:03:35.485
We need a hospital.


00:03:35.487 --> 00:03:37.189
Closest hospital's
two hours away.


00:03:42.360 --> 00:03:43.395
Bring her back here.


00:03:44.563 --> 00:03:45.696
It's okay, baby.


00:03:46.831 --> 00:03:47.666
There you go.


00:03:55.340 --> 00:03:56.474
Her pulse is strong.


00:03:58.810 --> 00:04:00.178
She's breathing steady now.


00:04:01.513 --> 00:04:04.416
From what you said on the phone,
I'd say this is hypercapnia.


00:04:04.950 --> 00:04:07.383
But I never heard of anyone
getting carbon dioxide poisoning


00:04:07.385 --> 00:04:08.619
in an open field.


00:04:08.621 --> 00:04:10.422
Are you sure she wasn't
locked inside somewhere?


00:04:12.791 --> 00:04:15.091
- Cameroon.
- What's that, Miss?


00:04:15.093 --> 00:04:17.162
Oh, thank God.


00:04:17.597 --> 00:04:18.763
There she is.


00:04:19.898 --> 00:04:21.032
How's my baby girl?


00:04:22.067 --> 00:04:24.133
I'm not a baby, Dad.


00:04:24.135 --> 00:04:25.536
- Ash.
- I was afraid I wouldn't be able


00:04:25.538 --> 00:04:27.473
to finish my work
without my assistant.


00:04:33.646 --> 00:04:35.011
Do you have a computer
I can use?


00:04:35.013 --> 00:04:36.081
I need to check the Internet.


00:04:37.516 --> 00:04:38.417
Back here.


00:04:44.724 --> 00:04:48.057
There's this lake in Cameroon.


00:04:48.059 --> 00:04:49.928
- <i>Emergency alert.</i>
- Hey.


00:04:50.263 --> 00:04:51.129
Look at that.


00:04:51.863 --> 00:04:53.699
<i>Regular programming will resume</i>


00:04:53.865 --> 00:04:55.301
<i>following this breaking news.</i>


00:04:56.502 --> 00:04:59.505
<i>A mid-Pacific earthquake
has now been confirmed.</i>


00:05:00.273 --> 00:05:02.974
<i>There are growing reports
of a coastal disaster.</i>


00:05:03.942 --> 00:05:07.013
<i>What you're seeing is video
from our San Francisco affiliate</i>


00:05:07.313 --> 00:05:09.749
<i>just moments before
the satellite link went down.</i>


00:05:10.249 --> 00:05:13.252
<i>It seems everything south
of Sacramento has gone dark.</i>


00:05:13.653 --> 00:05:14.754
- Oh, my...
- <i>All phone,</i>


00:05:14.919 --> 00:05:16.920
<i>Internet and satellite
communication was lost</i>


00:05:16.922 --> 00:05:19.625
<i>almost simultaneously,
about a half hour ago.</i>


00:05:20.092 --> 00:05:21.625
What the hell is going on?


00:05:21.627 --> 00:05:23.093
<i>Earlier reports
of the possible collapse</i>


00:05:23.095 --> 00:05:26.497
<i>of the West Antarctic ice sheet
remain unconfirmed.</i>


00:05:26.499 --> 00:05:27.898
<i>...appears to be</i>


00:05:27.900 --> 00:05:29.400
<i>a major seismic event,</i>


00:05:29.402 --> 00:05:31.937
<i>and the situation
is still developing.</i>


00:05:32.438 --> 00:05:34.405
<i>What we know so far...</i>


00:05:34.407 --> 00:05:36.108
What is this?


00:06:20.287 --> 00:06:21.153
Hi.


00:06:27.794 --> 00:06:28.662
I'm Davis.


00:06:30.530 --> 00:06:32.630
No, I know it sounds like
a last name,


00:06:32.632 --> 00:06:33.500
but it's not.


00:06:33.999 --> 00:06:36.401
It's my first name.


00:06:36.403 --> 00:06:37.637
Oh, and this is Erin.


00:06:55.322 --> 00:06:57.288
I can't believe
they're sending us up in this.


00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:58.889
Is it even safe to fly?


00:06:58.891 --> 00:07:00.026
Erin, relax.


00:07:00.327 --> 00:07:02.894
If I could take off in a
Blackhawk under fire in Fallujah


00:07:02.896 --> 00:07:05.165
I think I can handle
News Chopper 9 with a hangover.


00:07:05.999 --> 00:07:06.967
Hangover?


00:07:27.454 --> 00:07:28.723
Get in the chopper, now.


00:07:30.457 --> 00:07:31.324
Now!


00:08:01.923 --> 00:08:03.689
It's like that
all the way up the coast.


00:08:03.691 --> 00:08:05.758
At least as far as we went,
anyway.


00:08:05.760 --> 00:08:07.526
And it couldn't have
just been a wave.


00:08:07.528 --> 00:08:08.763
It went on forever.


00:08:09.397 --> 00:08:12.431
Like the sea levels rose,
you know, but all at once.


00:08:12.433 --> 00:08:15.468
We headed inland at Santa Rosa,
refueled in Reno.


00:08:15.470 --> 00:08:16.769
But there was an earthquake
there, and it's


00:08:16.771 --> 00:08:18.773
- exactly the same in Boise.
- Boise?


00:08:19.440 --> 00:08:20.475
Well, where were you headed?


00:08:20.641 --> 00:08:22.210
Well, I've got family
in Bozeman, but...


00:08:22.910 --> 00:08:25.112
it looks like I pushed
my chopper a little too hard.


00:08:26.447 --> 00:08:28.347
Well, you're more than welcome
to stay here


00:08:28.349 --> 00:08:29.817
as long as you like.
You'll be safe.


00:08:31.219 --> 00:08:32.887
Mayor, that may not be the case.


00:08:34.055 --> 00:08:36.824
- Dr. Cavanaugh, was it?
- Karen.


00:08:38.092 --> 00:08:39.360
Have you ever heard
of Cameroon?


00:08:39.928 --> 00:08:41.126
Cameroon?


00:08:41.128 --> 00:08:43.062
Back in the '80s,
thousands of villagers


00:08:43.064 --> 00:08:44.699
near Lake Nyos were asphyxiated,


00:08:45.099 --> 00:08:46.200
just like Barnes's sheep.


00:08:46.935 --> 00:08:48.369
It was carbon dioxide, it...


00:08:48.636 --> 00:08:50.669
hovers off the ground no more
than three or four feet,


00:08:50.671 --> 00:08:53.307
which is why
Ashley was affected, but not us.


00:08:54.041 --> 00:08:54.910
What's causing it?


00:08:57.678 --> 00:09:00.481
Lake Nyos is in the crater
of a dormant volcano.


00:09:00.716 --> 00:09:02.818
- We don't have a volcano.
- That's not true.


00:09:03.451 --> 00:09:05.319
Yellowstone is 90 miles
from here.


00:09:06.153 --> 00:09:07.355
All those hot springs?


00:09:07.823 --> 00:09:10.358
I mean, that place
is one giant volcano.


00:09:11.158 --> 00:09:13.629
You think Yellowstone's
a threat? Now?


00:09:14.362 --> 00:09:16.061
Look, I am just trying
to piece together


00:09:16.063 --> 00:09:17.564
what happened
to Ashley, the sheep,


00:09:17.566 --> 00:09:18.767
and now their story.


00:09:19.100 --> 00:09:21.400
How does a tsunami
have anything to do


00:09:21.402 --> 00:09:23.070
with a volcano and dead sheep?


00:09:25.339 --> 00:09:29.009
The news report... that was on
before the TV went out.


00:09:29.011 --> 00:09:31.613
It said that there was
a massive underwater earthquake,


00:09:31.914 --> 00:09:33.615
which would explain the tsunami.


00:09:34.048 --> 00:09:36.550
The weight of that much water
shifting on tectonic plates


00:09:36.552 --> 00:09:38.852
could strain Yellowstone
to the breaking point.


00:09:38.854 --> 00:09:40.754
Okay, but you don't know this
for sure.


00:09:40.756 --> 00:09:42.556
After what I've seen today,


00:09:42.558 --> 00:09:43.859
I'd be inclined
to take any warning.


00:09:44.459 --> 00:09:46.493
Look, I wish someone
could tell me I'm wrong.


00:09:46.495 --> 00:09:48.129
Do we know
that everything's down?


00:09:48.730 --> 00:09:51.631
Landlines, cell phones,
Internet?


00:09:51.633 --> 00:09:53.769
How about a CB, or a ham radio?


00:09:56.505 --> 00:09:58.540
Oh, no, not him.


00:09:59.308 --> 00:10:00.909
Why does it always
have to be him?


00:10:06.181 --> 00:10:07.050
Friendly.


00:10:08.017 --> 00:10:09.985
Not one of these survivalists.


00:10:10.419 --> 00:10:12.552
Uh, please,
don't use that word.


00:10:12.554 --> 00:10:13.555
Or "prepper".


00:10:13.722 --> 00:10:16.258
Amos Cade!
It's Mayor Wally!


00:10:21.530 --> 00:10:22.397
Amos.


00:10:23.365 --> 00:10:26.101
- We're here because, well, I...
- I know why you're here.


00:10:26.936 --> 00:10:29.669
So y'all can just turn around
and back away from my property.


00:10:29.671 --> 00:10:32.207
- It's an emergency.
- Yeah, I'll say it is.


00:10:32.775 --> 00:10:33.742
Teotwawki.


00:10:34.443 --> 00:10:36.111
The end of the world
as we know it.


00:10:36.545 --> 00:10:38.378
I'll give you the count of ten,
Wally.


00:10:38.380 --> 00:10:40.482
State of Emergency rules,
I can confiscate it.


00:10:40.817 --> 00:10:43.318
Whoa, wait a minute. What,
are you trying to set him off?


00:10:44.053 --> 00:10:47.021
I knew when it finally happened,
I'd be getting an unwanted knock


00:10:47.023 --> 00:10:48.123
on my door, Wally.


00:10:48.958 --> 00:10:50.994
I just never figured you'd have
the guts to do it.


00:10:52.061 --> 00:10:53.261
Hi, Mr. Cade?


00:10:53.696 --> 00:10:56.766
My name's Dr. Karen Cavanaugh.
We need your help.


00:10:57.066 --> 00:10:58.034
Doctor, huh?


00:10:58.433 --> 00:11:00.737
Why don't you go ask
your insurance company for help?


00:11:01.938 --> 00:11:03.338
I'm not that kind of doctor.


00:11:03.773 --> 00:11:06.807
I'm a scientist, and I think
we might be in real danger here,


00:11:06.809 --> 00:11:08.678
so, if we could just use
your radio.


00:11:08.978 --> 00:11:10.178
You're unprepared.


00:11:10.780 --> 00:11:12.448
And it finally hits the fan,


00:11:12.782 --> 00:11:15.449
the phones and the computers
are down, and you figure


00:11:15.451 --> 00:11:17.420
you'll just confiscate
what's mine!


00:11:17.954 --> 00:11:20.790
I'm sorry, the Chief
shouldn't have said that.


00:11:22.291 --> 00:11:23.593
See, this concerns you, too.


00:11:23.893 --> 00:11:26.963
If I'm right, your safe house
might not be so safe after all.


00:11:27.263 --> 00:11:29.164
Don't patronize me, Doctor.


00:11:29.799 --> 00:11:31.666
I'm not one of these
country yokels.


00:11:31.668 --> 00:11:32.669
Yellowstone!


00:11:34.470 --> 00:11:36.039
She thinks it might be priming
to blow.


00:11:36.506 --> 00:11:38.372
I'm not a conspiracy nut,
either.


00:11:38.374 --> 00:11:39.308
Mr. Cade!


00:11:40.076 --> 00:11:42.979
Farmer Barnes lost a herd
of sheep to CO2 venting,


00:11:43.312 --> 00:11:45.581
an early warning sign
of volcanic activity.


00:11:51.788 --> 00:11:53.790
- You're sure about that?
- No.


00:11:55.025 --> 00:11:57.293
That's why I'd like to borrow
some time on your radio.


00:12:05.169 --> 00:12:08.105
Wally, you ought to let the
lady doctor do all your talking.


00:12:08.504 --> 00:12:09.605
And I'd lose the whirlybird.


00:12:10.440 --> 00:12:12.142
- I can still hear you!
- Yeah, I know.


00:12:13.110 --> 00:12:14.810
Anything yet?


00:12:14.812 --> 00:12:17.179
Just some crazy rumors
and conspiracy theories,


00:12:17.181 --> 00:12:19.181
though this is Cade's radio.


00:12:19.183 --> 00:12:21.449
- What do we know for sure?
- Nothing good.


00:12:21.451 --> 00:12:23.885
One guy claims that
Seattle's underwater,


00:12:23.887 --> 00:12:25.887
and Eastern Washington's
under Martial Law.


00:12:25.889 --> 00:12:27.723
Yeah, and there's talk
of a refugee crisis


00:12:27.725 --> 00:12:29.225
in New Mexico and Nevada.


00:12:29.893 --> 00:12:31.095
Anything about Yellowstone?


00:12:31.995 --> 00:12:33.697
Farmers east of Idaho Falls,


00:12:33.997 --> 00:12:36.230
west of Cody, Wyoming,
and south of Livingston,


00:12:36.232 --> 00:12:37.534
all with dead livestock.


00:12:38.068 --> 00:12:39.701
Nothing from the authorities?


00:12:39.703 --> 00:12:41.169
Just the Emergency
Broadcast recording


00:12:41.171 --> 00:12:42.873
on the military frequencies.


00:12:43.339 --> 00:12:44.775
Hope you're not counting
on the military.


00:12:45.142 --> 00:12:46.944
I did for two tours
in Afghanistan.


00:12:47.845 --> 00:12:49.177
Combat Infantry,


00:12:49.179 --> 00:12:51.480
Desert Storm '91,
whirlybird man.


00:12:51.482 --> 00:12:52.750
You're really good
with nicknames.


00:12:53.450 --> 00:12:56.487
Even without confirmation
from FEMA or Civil Defense...


00:12:57.521 --> 00:12:58.920
I think Karen's right.


00:12:58.922 --> 00:13:00.522
Says the high school
science teacher.


00:13:00.524 --> 00:13:02.457
Yeah, I think I know
what I'm talking about.


00:13:02.459 --> 00:13:04.626
You really think
Yellowstone's gonna blow?


00:13:04.628 --> 00:13:06.697
Even if it's not
a full-blown eruption,


00:13:07.264 --> 00:13:08.732
this valley could experience


00:13:09.200 --> 00:13:11.900
catastrophic quakes,
gas pockets,


00:13:11.902 --> 00:13:13.737
hydrothermal explosions.


00:13:15.005 --> 00:13:17.038
If the wind's blowing
in the wrong direction,


00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:19.343
an ash cloud could poison
the air, the reservoir,


00:13:20.277 --> 00:13:22.813
or more CO2 venting,
and one morning nobody wakes up.


00:13:23.747 --> 00:13:25.480
We've been reviewing
these geological maps.


00:13:25.482 --> 00:13:26.650
Our best bet is to head


00:13:26.817 --> 00:13:28.485
for higher ground
in the Rockies, north of here.


00:13:29.553 --> 00:13:30.621
Evacuate?


00:13:32.223 --> 00:13:33.290
If I'm right,


00:13:33.590 --> 00:13:35.826
everything within 100 miles
of the caldera is dead.


00:13:36.426 --> 00:13:39.730
No warning sign,
no time to evacuate, just dead.


00:13:41.331 --> 00:13:43.665
When it blew up last, what,
half a million years ago?


00:13:43.667 --> 00:13:45.034
Six hundred forty thousand.


00:13:45.036 --> 00:13:47.071
It was an area the size
of Los Angeles.


00:13:47.437 --> 00:13:50.006
It seared the earth as far as
the Tetons and south to Jackson.


00:13:50.008 --> 00:13:52.844
It was the equivalent
of 10,000 Mount St. Helens.


00:13:54.112 --> 00:13:55.677
With all due respect,
Dr. Cavanaugh,


00:13:55.679 --> 00:13:57.347
we're talking
about half a million years ago?


00:13:57.681 --> 00:14:00.116
Barnes's sheep died
two days ago!


00:14:00.118 --> 00:14:02.317
You wanna wait until lava's
rolling down Main Street?


00:14:02.319 --> 00:14:05.320
Look...
this thing is fed


00:14:05.322 --> 00:14:08.224
by a molten magma hot spot
underneath the Earth's crust.


00:14:08.226 --> 00:14:10.226
It extends in
a southwest direction


00:14:10.228 --> 00:14:11.928
across Idaho-Montana border.


00:14:11.930 --> 00:14:13.631
We are right in the line
of fire.


00:14:14.098 --> 00:14:15.633
How much time do we have?


00:14:20.872 --> 00:14:22.707
Even if I had USGS data...


00:14:23.942 --> 00:14:25.143
it would still be a guess.


00:14:29.447 --> 00:14:31.616
Karen, what do you think?


00:14:38.656 --> 00:14:41.025
- Twenty-four hours.
- Twenty-four hours?


00:14:41.359 --> 00:14:42.825
I'd say go now,


00:14:42.827 --> 00:14:44.696
if I thought that was
remotely possible.


00:15:01.679 --> 00:15:03.548
Mayor! You gotta come see this.


00:15:36.081 --> 00:15:38.715
Everybody calm down.
Please, one at a time.


00:15:38.717 --> 00:15:40.384
I can't just leave my farm.


00:15:40.386 --> 00:15:42.755
Mr. Barnes, what happened to
your sheep was a warning sign.


00:15:43.655 --> 00:15:46.290
Our best bet is to head north
into the mountains


00:15:46.292 --> 00:15:47.758
for the protection
of the granite bedrock.


00:15:47.760 --> 00:15:50.559
Why not a city?
Spokane, or Boise?


00:15:50.561 --> 00:15:51.730
Of course.
Yeah, yeah.


00:15:53.132 --> 00:15:54.300
The coast is flooded,


00:15:54.633 --> 00:15:56.936
and the inland cities are choked
with refugees.


00:15:57.703 --> 00:15:58.771
And I saw Boise.


00:15:59.705 --> 00:16:00.839
It's a hole in the ground.


00:16:01.073 --> 00:16:03.941
Who ordered this evacuation?
Is it a federal thing?


00:16:03.943 --> 00:16:05.411
Well, actually,


00:16:06.178 --> 00:16:08.745
- I'm ordering it.
- Oh, Wally, why?


00:16:08.747 --> 00:16:11.817
Mayor, are you sure about this?


00:16:12.117 --> 00:16:14.117
Shouldn't we wait until
we contact the authorities?


00:16:14.119 --> 00:16:16.253
Wait until when,
until it's too late?


00:16:16.255 --> 00:16:17.721
I was in San Francisco!


00:16:17.723 --> 00:16:21.124
- We had no warning!
- You really think my dead sheep


00:16:21.126 --> 00:16:22.761
means we gotta evacuate
the whole town?


00:16:24.163 --> 00:16:25.030
I do.


00:16:25.965 --> 00:16:29.235
You all saw the giant crack
outside the school.


00:16:30.536 --> 00:16:34.272
We stay here, we die. Out there,
at least we have a chance.


00:16:37.377 --> 00:16:39.179
Everybody calm down.


00:16:39.812 --> 00:16:41.578
We don't need someone else


00:16:41.580 --> 00:16:43.350
to tell us how to react
to a crisis.


00:16:43.749 --> 00:16:46.819
We are intelligent people
who can reason and deduce.


00:16:49.189 --> 00:16:50.520
I don't need
a government committee


00:16:50.522 --> 00:16:52.256
to tell me when I'm in danger.


00:16:53.659 --> 00:16:56.329
Don't wait for someone else
to hand it to you.


00:16:57.496 --> 00:16:59.366
Be the hero of your own story.


00:17:12.879 --> 00:17:13.847
I'll be right back.


00:17:17.183 --> 00:17:20.351
Final preparations for
the evacuation of Pleasant Creek


00:17:20.353 --> 00:17:21.321
are now underway.


00:17:23.655 --> 00:17:24.590
Exodus.


00:17:26.525 --> 00:17:30.795
Residents are gathering all the
food, water and medical supplies


00:17:30.797 --> 00:17:34.000
they can carry for the exodus
of Pleasant Creek.


00:17:34.334 --> 00:17:36.134
She does know
that she's not on the air?


00:17:36.136 --> 00:17:37.704
Yeah, but someone's
gotta tell the story, right?


00:17:38.171 --> 00:17:39.606
Let's just hope someone's left
to hear it.


00:17:40.874 --> 00:17:42.609
Grab anything non-perishable.


00:17:43.043 --> 00:17:46.046
And see if you can find
first-aid kits in the pharmacy.


00:17:47.047 --> 00:17:48.748
Oh, I know
what you're gonna say.


00:17:49.716 --> 00:17:51.419
You have to find a way
to make everyone go.


00:17:52.652 --> 00:17:53.853
What more can we say?


00:17:54.488 --> 00:17:56.254
You want me to force people
to go?


00:17:56.256 --> 00:17:58.058
I don't have
that kind of manpower.


00:17:59.059 --> 00:18:01.393
All I can do
is order the evacuation.


00:18:01.395 --> 00:18:02.860
I can't force people to do it.


00:18:02.862 --> 00:18:04.729
There has to be something
we can do.


00:18:06.400 --> 00:18:07.801
Are you sure we're doing
the right thing?


00:18:08.269 --> 00:18:09.600
Maybe we are overreacting.


00:18:09.602 --> 00:18:11.971
Oh, come on, Wally.
Not you, too!


00:18:24.951 --> 00:18:25.919
I hope it's enough.


00:18:26.520 --> 00:18:28.389
I mean this is gonna be the most
valuable resource out there.


00:18:28.855 --> 00:18:30.091
People might even kill for it.


00:18:30.524 --> 00:18:32.393
What do you think they're gonna
do when the food runs out?


00:18:32.892 --> 00:18:33.760
The water?


00:18:34.195 --> 00:18:35.593
Just get them to the mountains,
all right?


00:18:35.595 --> 00:18:37.196
You'll figure out
the rest as you go along.


00:18:37.198 --> 00:18:39.233
Just face one disaster
at a time.


00:18:40.034 --> 00:18:41.235
You mean, as we go...


00:18:42.203 --> 00:18:43.070
right?


00:18:47.041 --> 00:18:48.008
You're not coming?


00:18:48.242 --> 00:18:50.044
I've got a sister and nephew
in Bozeman.


00:18:51.579 --> 00:18:53.514
I... I gotta see
if they're all right.


00:18:57.952 --> 00:18:59.251
Just keep an eye on Cade.


00:19:01.555 --> 00:19:02.556
He's all bluster.


00:19:03.124 --> 00:19:05.159
He might be playing nice
now, but if things get rough,


00:19:05.526 --> 00:19:07.294
he could be
a very dangerous man.


00:19:09.296 --> 00:19:10.664
That's what's dangerous.


00:19:11.132 --> 00:19:13.868
A little spark or something,
a lightning strike,


00:19:14.335 --> 00:19:15.936
and it's a rolling death trap.


00:19:16.571 --> 00:19:18.403
I wish you were driving it.


00:19:18.405 --> 00:19:19.406
Well, thanks.


00:19:22.676 --> 00:19:24.343
I may have flown Blackhawks
in Afghanistan,


00:19:24.345 --> 00:19:25.644
but even I'm afraid of this.


00:19:27.848 --> 00:19:28.782
What?


00:19:29.817 --> 00:19:31.451
Erin said to time how long
it took you


00:19:31.453 --> 00:19:32.487
to bring up Blackhawks.


00:19:37.658 --> 00:19:38.627
They'll listen to you.


00:19:40.161 --> 00:19:41.829
- How do you know?
- Because I would.


00:19:47.302 --> 00:19:48.901
What's going on?


00:19:48.903 --> 00:19:50.804
I'll give you two guesses,
but you'll only need one.


00:19:51.105 --> 00:19:52.006
Cade?


00:19:55.876 --> 00:19:58.278
<i>Jesús Cristo!</i> Cade!


00:19:58.280 --> 00:19:59.648
What the hell
are you guys doing?


00:20:00.014 --> 00:20:01.216
Protecting what's mine.


00:20:01.815 --> 00:20:02.983
They're trying to steal
from me.


00:20:03.318 --> 00:20:05.986
Nobody's stealing from you,
you crazy bastard.


00:20:06.421 --> 00:20:07.986
We're just taking inventory!


00:20:07.988 --> 00:20:09.823
What's mine is for me
and my own.


00:20:10.125 --> 00:20:11.560
What if I felt that way?


00:20:12.561 --> 00:20:14.394
You're not gonna
sweet talk me, darling.


00:20:14.396 --> 00:20:15.829
You ain't got nothing
to protect.


00:20:16.897 --> 00:20:18.665
Without the rule of law,


00:20:18.667 --> 00:20:21.334
first they come begging,
then they come demanding.


00:20:21.336 --> 00:20:23.138
Well, your welfare state
is over.


00:20:23.804 --> 00:20:26.472
You can't take what's mine just
because you didn't think ahead.


00:20:26.474 --> 00:20:27.741
Look, Cade...


00:20:28.410 --> 00:20:29.876
we're all in this together!


00:20:29.878 --> 00:20:32.214
Says those
with nothing to contribute.


00:20:32.981 --> 00:20:35.682
You just figured since you could
sucker me out of my radio,


00:20:35.684 --> 00:20:36.885
that I was just a sucker.


00:20:53.969 --> 00:20:54.903
Go ahead...


00:20:56.071 --> 00:20:57.072
take your shot.


00:21:03.278 --> 00:21:04.179
Don't.


00:21:10.385 --> 00:21:12.622
- Hey, hey.
- Is this it? Is it happening?


00:21:15.257 --> 00:21:16.124
Where you going?


00:21:16.692 --> 00:21:17.627
Hey!


00:21:20.161 --> 00:21:21.763
Who's gonna help me
carry all this stuff?


00:21:29.305 --> 00:21:30.171
Get in the cars!


00:21:34.042 --> 00:21:35.611
Get into the lead truck and go!


00:21:38.447 --> 00:21:40.347
We can't get out of here
unless it's moving! Go!


00:21:40.349 --> 00:21:41.217
Karen!


00:21:42.718 --> 00:21:44.287
- I'll get the fuel truck.
- Thank you.


00:21:44.654 --> 00:21:45.820
Chief! Chief!


00:21:47.822 --> 00:21:49.258
Help me out, man!


00:21:56.198 --> 00:21:57.933
Ashley! Are you hurt?


00:22:00.903 --> 00:22:02.938
Mr. Barnes! Mr. Barnes.


00:22:15.117 --> 00:22:18.054
Cade, come on! Come on!


00:22:21.657 --> 00:22:22.693
Open the door!


00:22:24.761 --> 00:22:25.796
Go, go, go!


00:22:46.783 --> 00:22:47.983
- No!
- Karen?


00:22:48.452 --> 00:22:49.686
We have to save them!


00:22:51.987 --> 00:22:54.156
- How many lost?
- I don't know,


00:22:54.624 --> 00:22:55.891
but we can't stop here.


00:22:56.360 --> 00:22:58.192
Well maybe I should go back.
I can get in a truck


00:22:58.194 --> 00:22:59.327
and I can see
if there's anybody...-


00:22:59.329 --> 00:23:01.331
Karen! There's nothing
to go back to.


00:23:03.999 --> 00:23:05.535
That's why
you have to keep it together.


00:23:06.737 --> 00:23:07.771
We gotta keep moving.


00:24:01.558 --> 00:24:02.426
How's Ashley?


00:24:03.861 --> 00:24:04.995
Sam and Diane are with her.


00:24:05.730 --> 00:24:06.963
She's pretty broken up.


00:24:09.634 --> 00:24:11.700
You too scared to keep riding
the death trap?


00:24:15.573 --> 00:24:16.473
I gotta go.


00:24:18.743 --> 00:24:19.677
I understand.


00:24:22.112 --> 00:24:23.481
I know how to get
to Triple Divide.


00:24:25.115 --> 00:24:26.451
Maybe I'll see you there.


00:24:28.753 --> 00:24:30.220
Take care of yourself, Davis.


00:24:35.058 --> 00:24:36.293
Remember what I said about Cade.


00:24:56.214 --> 00:24:57.181
Where's he going?


00:24:58.416 --> 00:25:00.351
Something he needs to find out
for himself.


00:25:02.587 --> 00:25:03.521
Is he coming back?


00:25:09.627 --> 00:25:10.628
I don't think so.


00:25:17.335 --> 00:25:18.603
<i>So it looks like we take the...</i>


00:25:19.237 --> 00:25:20.838
I-15 to Dillon...


00:25:21.472 --> 00:25:23.876
then take, uh, Highway 43.


00:25:25.376 --> 00:25:26.377
Uh, hold on.


00:25:28.981 --> 00:25:30.047
See, the problem is,


00:25:30.648 --> 00:25:31.984
all this through here...


00:25:32.951 --> 00:25:35.186
that's more dangerous
than where we came.


00:25:35.787 --> 00:25:38.055
I guess we could get
off the I-15...


00:25:38.957 --> 00:25:40.726
on 278, and loop around.


00:25:41.325 --> 00:25:42.959
I just don't know any other way


00:25:42.961 --> 00:25:45.296
that doesn't take us on the I-15
at least part of the way.


00:25:45.964 --> 00:25:46.999
I do.


00:25:48.967 --> 00:25:50.468
Where's your bad area, Doctor?


00:25:55.540 --> 00:25:56.407
Okay, that's easy.


00:25:57.341 --> 00:26:00.512
You take Blacktail up to Dillon
over the 278.


00:26:01.212 --> 00:26:02.679
It keeps you off the I-15.


00:26:02.681 --> 00:26:04.081
Yeah, but how do we get
to Blacktail?


00:26:05.049 --> 00:26:07.553
There's a mining access road
that runs parallel...


00:26:08.386 --> 00:26:11.053
just past the next junction,
nine or ten miles up.


00:26:11.055 --> 00:26:13.088
How do you know about that?


00:26:13.090 --> 00:26:15.360
I was looking at some land
up there for a B.O.L.


00:26:15.694 --> 00:26:17.261
I got priced out
by some Hollywood types.


00:26:17.863 --> 00:26:19.998
I have absolutely no idea
what you just said.


00:26:20.632 --> 00:26:22.367
B.O.L.
is a bug-out location.


00:26:22.734 --> 00:26:26.369
I did a story on one of those
"Prepper" apocalypse shows.


00:26:26.371 --> 00:26:28.072
Yeah, those shows
are all garbage.


00:26:28.540 --> 00:26:31.508
- It's propaganda. See preppers...
- Are you sure about this road,


00:26:31.510 --> 00:26:33.345
uh, in the property
that you bought?


00:26:33.912 --> 00:26:35.514
I didn't buy it.
I couldn't afford it.


00:26:36.113 --> 00:26:38.315
You know, if Yellowstone
is so dangerous,


00:26:38.317 --> 00:26:40.118
why is the land there
so expensive?


00:26:40.552 --> 00:26:42.218
I thought this whole
volcano thing


00:26:42.220 --> 00:26:43.587
was just a real estate scam,


00:26:43.589 --> 00:26:45.490
a cover story
to scare people off, you know?


00:26:45.924 --> 00:26:47.025
A conspiracy, huh?


00:26:49.361 --> 00:26:50.262
Blacktail,


00:26:50.996 --> 00:26:51.930
two-seventy-eight.


00:26:52.564 --> 00:26:53.432
I'm sure.


00:26:56.902 --> 00:26:57.769
Amos.


00:26:58.737 --> 00:26:59.605
Doc.


00:27:00.305 --> 00:27:02.307
I'm really glad to have
somebody like you on our team.


00:27:05.277 --> 00:27:06.543
We're not on the same team.


00:27:06.545 --> 00:27:08.213
We're just travelling
in the same direction.


00:27:22.427 --> 00:27:23.662
Time to eat, guys.


00:27:23.930 --> 00:27:26.298
We lost a lot of the food,
so make it last.


00:27:27.332 --> 00:27:28.266
There you go.


00:27:29.401 --> 00:27:30.302
And for you.


00:27:36.375 --> 00:27:38.011
- You doing okay, sweetie?
- Yeah.


00:27:38.945 --> 00:27:39.812
There you are.


00:27:40.546 --> 00:27:41.413
Thanks.


00:27:41.814 --> 00:27:43.049
Why does she get so much?


00:27:44.117 --> 00:27:45.217
She's ten.


00:27:47.920 --> 00:27:50.322
Every time I think there's
a decent human being in there...


00:27:51.223 --> 00:27:53.358
he does everything he can
to prove me wrong.


00:30:07.494 --> 00:30:08.529
Hey!


00:30:10.098 --> 00:30:11.963
Get outta here, man!
This house is mine!


00:30:11.965 --> 00:30:13.698
This house belongs
to my sister!


00:30:13.700 --> 00:30:15.803
Nothing belongs to nobody
no more.


00:30:16.904 --> 00:30:18.672
Trust me, you don't wanna
be here.


00:30:19.807 --> 00:30:21.439
No, you don't!


00:30:23.844 --> 00:30:24.944
Hurry up, man!


00:31:07.655 --> 00:31:10.024
Get out of my house.


00:31:14.361 --> 00:31:17.232
Look, we saw nobody here,
that's the truth.


00:31:18.032 --> 00:31:19.300
Empty your pockets now.


00:31:19.667 --> 00:31:20.602
- Look...
- Now!


00:31:22.003 --> 00:31:23.538
Okay. Here you go.


00:33:13.782 --> 00:33:15.017
Stop!


00:33:23.926 --> 00:33:24.860
What do we do?


00:33:27.596 --> 00:33:29.698
Nothing we can do.
No one could survive that.


00:33:30.300 --> 00:33:31.334
Oh, good God!


00:33:33.136 --> 00:33:34.634
We gotta get off this ridge


00:33:34.636 --> 00:33:36.304
before there's
another earthquake.


00:33:36.306 --> 00:33:37.307
Back in the truck.


00:33:41.311 --> 00:33:42.979
He's right, Karen. We gotta go.


00:35:01.258 --> 00:35:02.926
<i>...you let yourselves be ruled!</i>


00:35:03.593 --> 00:35:04.892
<i>You wanted to feel safe</i>


00:35:04.894 --> 00:35:06.596
<i>under the skirts
of mother government.</i>


00:35:07.231 --> 00:35:08.430
<i>To feed and clothe you...</i>


00:35:08.432 --> 00:35:10.134
How can he be
the only one broadcasting?


00:35:10.568 --> 00:35:13.237
Does anybody actually believe
all this crap?


00:35:13.770 --> 00:35:15.571
<i>...in exchange for an empty</i>


00:35:15.573 --> 00:35:16.873
<i>promise of security.</i>


00:35:17.942 --> 00:35:19.243
<i>Where's that security now?</i>


00:35:20.177 --> 00:35:22.277
<i>Where's the government
that said it would protect you?</i>


00:35:22.279 --> 00:35:24.012
Finally someone speaking
the truth.


00:35:24.014 --> 00:35:25.950
Damn straight.


00:35:26.450 --> 00:35:27.950
<i>They're all holed up in their</i>


00:35:27.952 --> 00:35:31.255
<i>mountaintop fortresses
or their private space stations,</i>


00:35:31.754 --> 00:35:33.322
<i>just waiting for the rest of us</i>


00:35:33.324 --> 00:35:35.758
<i>to go feral and destroy
each other.</i>


00:35:36.494 --> 00:35:38.127
- Hey.
- Hey.


00:35:38.129 --> 00:35:39.495
You mind taking this to Ashley?


00:35:39.497 --> 00:35:40.829
- Oh, yeah, no problem.
- Thanks.


00:35:40.831 --> 00:35:41.799
All right. See you later.


00:36:04.955 --> 00:36:06.023
Where'd you find that?


00:36:09.461 --> 00:36:10.661
Hey, pass it here.


00:36:21.972 --> 00:36:23.308
You're holding out on us?


00:36:24.909 --> 00:36:26.609
Amos Cade,
I'm disappointed in you.


00:36:26.611 --> 00:36:27.445
Darling,


00:36:28.112 --> 00:36:30.147
share and share alike ain't
how this is gonna play out.


00:36:31.081 --> 00:36:32.683
Now, you're a smart girl.
You know that.


00:36:33.884 --> 00:36:35.187
We need to work together.


00:36:37.922 --> 00:36:39.723
Hey.


00:36:40.358 --> 00:36:41.692
Now, I told you before...


00:36:42.726 --> 00:36:44.329
what's mine is for me
and my own.


00:37:01.279 --> 00:37:02.180
I thought so.


00:37:06.251 --> 00:37:08.420
Why don't you just scamper off
back to camp?


00:37:08.719 --> 00:37:10.956
You can keep playing
Commander in Chief all you want.


00:37:11.755 --> 00:37:13.058
Just remember one thing.


00:37:14.725 --> 00:37:16.461
Ain't no one ever
ruled over me...


00:37:17.362 --> 00:37:18.430
and no one ever will.


00:37:23.335 --> 00:37:25.070
Well, go on.
What are you waiting for?


00:37:28.840 --> 00:37:29.908
She's waiting on me.


00:37:32.744 --> 00:37:33.745
Hi, Davis.


00:37:34.412 --> 00:37:35.413
I missed a lot.


00:37:37.617 --> 00:37:38.817
Mr. Whirlybird.


00:37:40.720 --> 00:37:42.887
Let's see if you have the guts
to pull the trigger.


00:37:45.890 --> 00:37:47.125
I ain't afraid of dying.


00:37:49.428 --> 00:37:51.396
Anyone who stockpiles guns,


00:37:52.197 --> 00:37:53.131
hoards food,


00:37:53.898 --> 00:37:56.968
and booby-traps his own home
is terrified of dying.


00:37:57.670 --> 00:38:00.537
It's okay, Davis. It was just
a little misunderstanding.


00:38:00.539 --> 00:38:01.739
He was pointing a gun at you!


00:38:01.741 --> 00:38:03.208
And now
you're pointing one at him.


00:38:04.710 --> 00:38:06.144
Let's just call this even and...


00:38:07.045 --> 00:38:08.581
talk about it tomorrow
with clear heads.


00:38:14.453 --> 00:38:15.920
Ain't nothing to talk about.


00:38:18.624 --> 00:38:19.525
Doc.


00:38:21.527 --> 00:38:24.163
I took your measure tonight.
I know how far you'll go.


00:38:28.933 --> 00:38:30.802
You can't say the same thing
for me.


00:38:31.537 --> 00:38:34.640
You remember that the next time
you sneak up on me in the dark.


00:38:37.643 --> 00:38:38.511
Let's go.


00:39:18.685 --> 00:39:19.885
Are we safe here?


00:39:20.319 --> 00:39:21.588
I don't know if anywhere
is safe.


00:39:23.490 --> 00:39:25.792
Let's just hope
whatever's gonna happen here...


00:39:26.793 --> 00:39:27.728
already happened.


00:39:30.764 --> 00:39:31.765
Do you hear that?


00:39:32.031 --> 00:39:33.667
Is that...


00:39:33.999 --> 00:39:37.336
- There! Hey! Hey!
- Down here!


00:39:43.810 --> 00:39:45.746
We're here!
We're down here!


00:39:46.245 --> 00:39:47.581
Please! No!


00:41:11.566 --> 00:41:13.166
It's Ashley!


00:41:16.970 --> 00:41:18.773
- Ashley!
- Karen!


00:41:21.074 --> 00:41:21.943
Karen!


00:41:23.344 --> 00:41:26.046
- What happened? Ashley screamed!
- That was him.


00:41:26.781 --> 00:41:28.112
Uh, it's my fault.


00:41:28.114 --> 00:41:29.650
I caught them off guard.
I didn't mean to scare them!


00:41:34.622 --> 00:41:35.756
What are you doing here?


00:41:36.156 --> 00:41:37.959
Exercising my right
to free speech.


00:41:38.124 --> 00:41:39.293
Wait a second.


00:41:42.430 --> 00:41:43.965
You're the conspiracy guy.


00:41:44.665 --> 00:41:45.600
The one on the radio.


00:41:46.167 --> 00:41:50.035
Conspiracy guy? That's what I
get, "conspiracy guy"?


00:41:50.037 --> 00:41:53.841
Hmph.
Yeah, well, yeah, that's me.


00:41:54.977 --> 00:41:56.611
I used to broadcast
out of my house


00:41:57.211 --> 00:41:59.280
until they figured out
what I was all about


00:41:59.580 --> 00:42:00.648
and my place was bugged.


00:42:01.315 --> 00:42:03.986
Harassing phone calls,
black helicopters. Shh!


00:42:07.088 --> 00:42:08.356
Maybe they did me a favor.


00:42:08.991 --> 00:42:10.993
If I wasn't here when the whole
damn town went to hell,


00:42:11.759 --> 00:42:14.262
- I wouldn't be here at all.
- Do you know what's going on?


00:42:14.997 --> 00:42:15.898
What happened?


00:42:16.264 --> 00:42:19.200
Well, I... I won't pretend
that it isn't bad.


00:42:21.003 --> 00:42:21.870
It's bad.


00:42:22.804 --> 00:42:23.906
Oh, wait, but I can show you!


00:42:26.173 --> 00:42:28.509
I was able to download these


00:42:28.744 --> 00:42:30.077
before the grid collapsed.


00:42:36.350 --> 00:42:37.719
This can't be possible.


00:42:38.820 --> 00:42:39.988
It's really all gone.


00:42:44.626 --> 00:42:46.929
I just can't believe
it's really this bad.


00:42:47.930 --> 00:42:50.432
We all know this was man-made,
right?


00:42:51.900 --> 00:42:53.702
They let this happen on purpose.


00:42:55.102 --> 00:42:56.371
They knew.


00:43:17.793 --> 00:43:19.394
I hate to say
"I told you so"...


00:43:20.629 --> 00:43:21.830
but I told you so.


00:43:22.898 --> 00:43:24.700
I mean, I've been talking
about this for years.


00:43:25.067 --> 00:43:25.934
For years!


00:43:26.969 --> 00:43:29.102
What about the rest
of the world?


00:43:29.104 --> 00:43:31.538
Have you heard
about anything from Europe


00:43:31.540 --> 00:43:34.077
- or... or Asia?
- Total blackout.


00:43:35.611 --> 00:43:36.878
It's exactly what they want,


00:43:37.779 --> 00:43:38.880
everyone in the dark.


00:43:40.182 --> 00:43:41.550
Who exactly are "they"?


00:43:42.684 --> 00:43:44.286
Them! The royal "they".


00:43:45.120 --> 00:43:47.422
The Illuminati.
The New World Order.


00:43:48.490 --> 00:43:50.292
Puppet masters
that control everyone.


00:43:50.994 --> 00:43:55.832
- CIA, DARPA, the... the Kremlin.
- And what exactly do they do?


00:43:56.833 --> 00:43:57.767
Area 51.


00:43:58.600 --> 00:44:03.338
MK Ultra. GM crop manipulation.
Weather control. Mind control!


00:44:04.107 --> 00:44:05.607
You think that's fluoride
in the water?


00:44:06.475 --> 00:44:07.777
And the damn chem-trails,


00:44:08.577 --> 00:44:10.044
pumping chemicals in
the atmosphere,


00:44:10.046 --> 00:44:11.277
making us all impotent.


00:44:13.582 --> 00:44:15.116
Maybe they're
making you impotent, Sutton,


00:44:15.118 --> 00:44:16.919
but my gear works out just fine.


00:44:19.521 --> 00:44:21.589
No, Vince, this is where you
and I disagree.


00:44:21.591 --> 00:44:23.423
I just don't believe
that the government workers


00:44:23.425 --> 00:44:25.528
are clever enough
to run a conspiracy.


00:44:26.261 --> 00:44:27.697
They sure as hell
don't care enough.


00:44:31.266 --> 00:44:33.235
I actually agree with you,
Mr. Cade.


00:44:34.103 --> 00:44:36.304
Did you assume
I was just a conspiracy nut?


00:45:00.830 --> 00:45:02.065
I wanna go home.


00:45:03.332 --> 00:45:04.200
Oh.


00:45:05.234 --> 00:45:06.369
Me too, sweetie.


00:45:07.171 --> 00:45:08.805
Where we're going
is gonna be our new home.


00:45:09.472 --> 00:45:10.339
You'll see.


00:45:13.543 --> 00:45:15.545
I'm gonna be outside, okay?


00:45:16.312 --> 00:45:18.015
If you need anything,
you just call out.


00:45:18.949 --> 00:45:20.683
Are you gonna come back?


00:45:21.185 --> 00:45:22.351
Of course, I will.


00:45:23.553 --> 00:45:25.755
Whatever happens,
we stick together, right?


00:45:27.824 --> 00:45:28.892
You're my assistant.


00:45:36.566 --> 00:45:37.533
Get some sleep.


00:45:57.020 --> 00:45:59.223
The Antarctic is in
the south, right.


00:45:59.455 --> 00:46:02.126
And there's, uh,
an ancient...


00:46:02.760 --> 00:46:05.193
Like, that might have been
before the planet


00:46:05.195 --> 00:46:08.532
shifted on its axis
and the ice cap moved.


00:46:09.365 --> 00:46:11.566
That was like,
it could've been Atlantis,


00:46:11.568 --> 00:46:12.970
Lemuria or the moon or...


00:46:13.403 --> 00:46:15.539
But anyway,
it was like a major...


00:46:16.774 --> 00:46:17.708
alien base.


00:46:17.941 --> 00:46:19.409
You missed
all the conspiracy talk.


00:46:19.843 --> 00:46:20.711
Lucky me.


00:46:25.749 --> 00:46:27.651
Hey, I wanted to thank you
for coming back.


00:46:27.951 --> 00:46:29.086
You saved my ass.


00:46:35.659 --> 00:46:37.461
What's he doing?
What is all this?


00:46:38.495 --> 00:46:39.830
Winning hearts and minds.


00:46:40.597 --> 00:46:42.397
I'm not sure what his play is,
but I'm pretty sure


00:46:42.399 --> 00:46:44.501
he's laying the groundwork for
a <i>coup d'état.</i>


00:46:47.404 --> 00:46:48.305
Hey, everyone...


00:46:49.473 --> 00:46:51.508
I got a little surprise
I've been saving.


00:46:52.243 --> 00:46:53.944
Thought I might share
with you all.


00:46:55.280 --> 00:46:57.681
Why do I have such a bad feeling
about this?


00:46:59.817 --> 00:47:00.717
'Cause you're smart.


00:47:02.786 --> 00:47:03.787
I'm glad you're here.


00:47:24.843 --> 00:47:25.977
- Ashley!
- The gas!


00:47:29.613 --> 00:47:30.715
Help me with the barrels!


00:47:31.548 --> 00:47:32.416
Come on!


00:47:39.824 --> 00:47:41.793
Hold on, sweetie. Put your arms
around my neck.


00:47:46.564 --> 00:47:48.430
Cover your head with this
and hold it tight!


00:47:48.432 --> 00:47:50.433
As tight as you can!
I'll be right back!


00:47:50.435 --> 00:47:52.335
Don't go! No!


00:47:58.810 --> 00:48:00.712
Go! Go this way!
Go this...


00:48:01.412 --> 00:48:03.715
No! No! No!


00:48:04.415 --> 00:48:06.885
Come here. Come here.


00:48:16.060 --> 00:48:18.496
Help him out! Help Davis!


00:48:18.830 --> 00:48:20.999
- Get away from that fire!
- No!


00:48:28.439 --> 00:48:30.441
Make it stop! Make it stop!


00:48:45.090 --> 00:48:46.125
Altogether, we've got...


00:48:46.992 --> 00:48:48.227
a dozen cans of food...


00:48:49.527 --> 00:48:50.795
a handful of water jugs.


00:48:52.898 --> 00:48:54.867
We should fill up what we can
before we get out of here.


00:48:55.901 --> 00:48:57.036
Let me see what I can do.


00:49:10.916 --> 00:49:11.817
Well, we...


00:49:12.583 --> 00:49:13.619
got the truck running, but...


00:49:14.420 --> 00:49:15.453
for how long, I don't know.


00:49:17.555 --> 00:49:20.125
Not enough fuel to get
two vehicles up there anyway.


00:49:21.860 --> 00:49:23.228
We'll figure something out,
Wally.


00:49:29.601 --> 00:49:30.669
Erin?


00:49:31.770 --> 00:49:33.038
Erin, you okay?


00:49:36.409 --> 00:49:37.343
I found this.


00:49:40.012 --> 00:49:41.947
Well, why don't you go see
if it'll do any good, sweetie?


00:50:16.882 --> 00:50:17.850
How is she?


00:50:47.080 --> 00:50:48.081
I found this.


00:51:01.394 --> 00:51:02.262
I...


00:51:03.163 --> 00:51:06.599
I'm serious. This is for like
a skinned knee or a paper cut.


00:51:08.034 --> 00:51:08.902
I just...


00:51:09.702 --> 00:51:11.704
I don't think there's
anything else I can do.


00:51:13.339 --> 00:51:16.076
She's already septic, and she's
burning up with a fever.


00:51:16.410 --> 00:51:18.412
Isn't there any... anything?


00:51:19.913 --> 00:51:21.449
Make her
more comfy, I guess.


00:51:22.182 --> 00:51:23.249
Is she in pain?


00:51:25.885 --> 00:51:28.254
I don't even think she knows
where she is.


00:51:32.560 --> 00:51:33.927
Isn't that cruel?


00:51:37.630 --> 00:51:39.097
I'm gonna go see if there's
some broth


00:51:39.099 --> 00:51:40.334
or something we can give her.


00:52:28.582 --> 00:52:29.517
Do it.


00:52:31.051 --> 00:52:32.520
It's the humane thing to do.


00:52:33.754 --> 00:52:36.121
You might as well pour
that broth on a pile of dirt


00:52:36.123 --> 00:52:38.225
and pray for flowers. Do it!


00:52:58.647 --> 00:52:59.813
Is everything okay?


00:53:00.615 --> 00:53:02.283
I just... Yeah.


00:53:07.355 --> 00:53:09.023
Cade's still in there with her.


00:53:10.625 --> 00:53:12.760
I'll go back.


00:53:23.572 --> 00:53:25.507
It was the right thing to do.
You all knew it.


00:53:26.040 --> 00:53:27.676
But no one had the courage
to do it.


00:53:28.042 --> 00:53:29.509
A leader's gotta be
willing to do


00:53:29.511 --> 00:53:30.811
what needs to be done.


00:53:31.346 --> 00:53:33.714
And that includes deciding
what to do with these bodies.


00:53:34.815 --> 00:53:36.318
Can't count
on any more pig meat.


00:53:38.620 --> 00:53:40.121
You son of a bitch!


00:53:44.059 --> 00:53:44.926
Davis!


00:53:48.930 --> 00:53:49.931
Please.


00:54:06.682 --> 00:54:08.850
Three days into those
mountains with no food...


00:54:09.851 --> 00:54:11.386
you'll realize the mistake
you made.


00:54:12.053 --> 00:54:14.456
No mistake. Choice.


00:54:15.223 --> 00:54:16.124
Not to be an animal.


00:54:18.561 --> 00:54:21.496
I don't take any joy in the idea
of eating human flesh...


00:54:22.732 --> 00:54:24.432
but if it's between that
and dying...


00:54:25.601 --> 00:54:27.769
I'll do whatever I have to do
to survive.


00:54:30.005 --> 00:54:32.475
See, that's a line that you
won't cross, but I will.


00:54:36.111 --> 00:54:38.547
And I'll outlive
every single one of you,


00:54:39.214 --> 00:54:40.215
and you know it.


00:54:42.083 --> 00:54:43.018
Get in the truck, Karen.


00:54:50.992 --> 00:54:52.593
You confiscating my gun?


00:54:52.595 --> 00:54:55.130
We gave you a fair share cut
of the supplies in the office.


00:54:55.464 --> 00:54:57.433
We need a gun
to defend ourselves!


00:54:57.799 --> 00:54:59.168
That's not my problem anymore.


00:55:04.640 --> 00:55:05.574
Damnit, Cade!


00:55:07.143 --> 00:55:08.711
- What do we do now?
- We follow them!


00:55:09.111 --> 00:55:10.011
On foot?


00:55:13.815 --> 00:55:16.619
- Know any shortcuts?
- I don't know any shortcuts.


00:55:17.153 --> 00:55:18.554
I'm a survivalist.


00:55:19.088 --> 00:55:19.955
I make them.


00:55:46.182 --> 00:55:47.983
Last of the food and the water.


00:55:48.685 --> 00:55:50.019
Save it for Ashley.


00:55:51.320 --> 00:55:53.589
We have no choice.
We need supplies.


00:55:55.024 --> 00:55:56.593
Then I guess we risk I-15.


00:55:58.327 --> 00:55:59.261
Hopefully, we'll...


00:56:00.496 --> 00:56:02.998
come across a truck stop
before too long.


00:57:01.024 --> 00:57:03.026
What is that?


00:57:03.827 --> 00:57:05.095
Ugh, sweet merciful heaven.


00:57:05.829 --> 00:57:07.431
Oh, she stinks.


00:57:10.333 --> 00:57:11.869
Looks like she killed herself.


00:57:18.542 --> 00:57:19.676
Check the glove box.


00:57:23.146 --> 00:57:24.014
Bingo.


00:57:24.481 --> 00:57:26.581
I'll never understand
what happens to a person,


00:57:26.583 --> 00:57:28.118
makes them lose their will
to survive.


00:57:29.119 --> 00:57:30.320
Some people just lose hope.


00:57:32.657 --> 00:57:35.158
It's not about hope, radio man.
It's about will.


00:57:36.627 --> 00:57:38.193
Time you should
start asking yourself,


00:57:38.195 --> 00:57:39.429
"How far are you willing to go?"


00:59:06.484 --> 00:59:08.854
Uh... guys?


00:59:10.856 --> 00:59:13.257
Somebody's already bypassed
the electronics.


00:59:15.293 --> 00:59:16.693
I think I can get
the pump working.


00:59:16.695 --> 00:59:17.729
Well, make it fast.


00:59:17.996 --> 00:59:19.430
Whoever set this up
could come back.


00:59:19.831 --> 00:59:21.365
We're not the only ones
looking for fuel.


00:59:23.569 --> 00:59:24.603
Somebody's coming!


00:59:25.671 --> 00:59:27.539
Just fill the pick-up.
We'll leave the truck!


00:59:28.941 --> 00:59:30.107
Maybe they're friendly.


00:59:30.776 --> 00:59:32.174
- We gotta go!
- What?


00:59:32.176 --> 00:59:33.677
We think somebody's
been living here.


00:59:33.679 --> 00:59:35.712
Yeah, I know, and they're back!
Come on, we gotta go now!


00:59:35.714 --> 00:59:37.214
Let's go, Ashley.
Let's go, sweetie.


00:59:38.917 --> 00:59:42.054
They're not friendly!
They're shooting arrows!


00:59:43.689 --> 00:59:46.923
Leave the truck! Get in!
Everybody in!


00:59:46.925 --> 00:59:49.226
We gotta go!
Come on! Come here!


00:59:49.528 --> 00:59:52.329
Vogel! Gotta go! We gotta go!


00:59:52.331 --> 00:59:53.599
Come on!


00:59:54.566 --> 00:59:56.566
Davis!


00:59:56.568 --> 00:59:57.736
Davis!


01:00:00.472 --> 01:00:01.974
Go! Go!


01:00:09.381 --> 01:00:10.582
Go, go, go, go!


01:00:24.196 --> 01:00:25.729
We gotta get that shaft out
of there.


01:00:29.301 --> 01:00:30.268
I'm serious.


01:00:30.669 --> 01:00:31.871
We leave it in,
it'll get infected.


01:00:32.437 --> 01:00:34.007
And if we take it out,
I bleed to death.


01:00:37.476 --> 01:00:38.543
Not a lot of good options here.


01:00:42.381 --> 01:00:43.348
Come here.


01:00:50.555 --> 01:00:51.924
Are you sure
we're still heading west?


01:00:52.257 --> 01:00:53.291
We're heading west.


01:00:54.060 --> 01:00:55.560
But how do you know?
I mean,


01:00:55.962 --> 01:00:57.193
this whole thing could be
some kind of


01:00:57.195 --> 01:00:58.798
magnetic reversal, right?


01:01:00.099 --> 01:01:01.999
North and south
switching polarities.


01:01:02.001 --> 01:01:03.636
Even compasses would be useless.


01:01:04.537 --> 01:01:06.539
The sun still sets in the west.


01:01:07.372 --> 01:01:08.206
Right.


01:01:12.244 --> 01:01:14.681
Are we taking a break?
I could sure use it.


01:01:15.815 --> 01:01:17.550
No breaks for you, Mr. Shortcut.


01:01:34.300 --> 01:01:35.234
How's he doing?


01:01:36.402 --> 01:01:37.503
We need a hospital.


01:01:39.305 --> 01:01:41.007
I sure wish Doc Rowe was here.


01:01:44.844 --> 01:01:45.745
Me, too.


01:01:52.819 --> 01:01:53.720
This...


01:01:54.520 --> 01:01:55.755
this wasn't here.


01:01:59.892 --> 01:02:00.760
Oh, no.


01:02:01.394 --> 01:02:02.462
Oh, man, this isn't good.


01:02:03.429 --> 01:02:05.899
We're gonna have to double back.
We can't get through this.


01:02:06.232 --> 01:02:08.969
- You promised me a shortcut.
- Well, I mean...


01:02:10.871 --> 01:02:11.771
I didn't know.


01:02:13.406 --> 01:02:14.906
How was I supposed to know?


01:02:14.908 --> 01:02:16.409
The hell are supposed
to do now, Cade?


01:02:17.010 --> 01:02:17.878
We keep moving.


01:02:18.644 --> 01:02:21.547
And we stop listening
to anything this dumbass says!


01:02:25.485 --> 01:02:26.687
How was I supposed to know?


01:02:27.386 --> 01:02:29.223
You better find
some hidden talents


01:02:29.522 --> 01:02:30.891
if you wanna stay useful to me.


01:02:46.106 --> 01:02:47.941
Wally, can you see well enough?


01:02:48.909 --> 01:02:49.977
Maybe we should stop,


01:02:50.177 --> 01:02:51.912
I'd rather see a cliff
before driving over it.


01:02:52.411 --> 01:02:54.114
It's thick,
but I can see.


01:02:55.249 --> 01:02:56.917
Ew. What's that smell?


01:02:58.418 --> 01:03:00.154
Like burning matches?


01:03:00.521 --> 01:03:01.822
That's sulfur dioxide.


01:03:02.923 --> 01:03:05.159
CO2 must be bonding
with the water vapor.


01:03:05.959 --> 01:03:07.225
Should I pull over,
wait it out?


01:03:07.227 --> 01:03:08.762
No, no, it can be toxic.


01:03:09.329 --> 01:03:12.099
Enough of a concentration,
you get sulfuric acid.


01:03:12.599 --> 01:03:14.134
Let's just see if we can push
through it, okay?


01:03:17.304 --> 01:03:18.472
Oh, what the hell!


01:03:19.039 --> 01:03:20.305
What happened now?


01:03:20.307 --> 01:03:22.342
I... I didn't do anything.
It just stopped.


01:03:22.876 --> 01:03:23.744
Pop the hood.


01:03:37.125 --> 01:03:39.593
- Are you okay?
- Keep the window closed.


01:03:39.994 --> 01:03:41.328
All the plastic
is melting!


01:03:44.765 --> 01:03:46.533
What? The car is melting!


01:03:47.835 --> 01:03:49.070
What the hell is this?


01:03:50.171 --> 01:03:52.339
- Sulfur dioxide...
- Whoa, Davis!


01:03:55.243 --> 01:03:56.211
I need help!


01:03:57.245 --> 01:03:59.147
Get outta here. Now! Go.


01:03:59.948 --> 01:04:00.882
Okay, come on.


01:04:12.160 --> 01:04:13.393
We have to find cover!


01:04:13.862 --> 01:04:15.196
Guys, over here!


01:04:15.897 --> 01:04:16.996
Over here!


01:04:16.998 --> 01:04:18.398
Over here!


01:04:35.683 --> 01:04:36.918
Is everyone okay?


01:04:37.585 --> 01:04:39.120
Davis doesn't look
too good.


01:04:41.256 --> 01:04:42.523
Let's move him further back.


01:04:45.361 --> 01:04:46.261
Davis?


01:04:47.195 --> 01:04:48.362
I'll be right there.


01:04:48.364 --> 01:04:49.464
- Wally!
- Where you going?


01:04:49.864 --> 01:04:51.298
- We need supplies!
- Wally, come back here!


01:04:51.300 --> 01:04:53.269
Wally, it's too dangerous!


01:04:55.470 --> 01:04:57.739
Wally! Damn it.
Should I go after him?


01:04:58.039 --> 01:04:59.040
No.


01:05:01.243 --> 01:05:02.278
Can you see him?


01:05:03.011 --> 01:05:04.846
Wally! Over here!


01:05:05.480 --> 01:05:07.615
- Walk straight! Wally!
- Wally, come here!


01:05:09.684 --> 01:05:10.618
Over here! Run!


01:05:11.419 --> 01:05:12.620
- This way!
- Oh!


01:05:13.421 --> 01:05:15.088
Wally, Wally.


01:05:15.090 --> 01:05:16.091
Sit down.


01:05:17.792 --> 01:05:19.727
It burns!
It's burning my eyes!


01:05:20.762 --> 01:05:21.763
Hold on, hold on!


01:05:22.830 --> 01:05:23.698
Oh, my eyes!


01:05:24.565 --> 01:05:25.566
I need a bandage!


01:05:26.168 --> 01:05:27.901
Water! Pour water on it!


01:05:27.903 --> 01:05:30.139
No, it's an acid.
It'll just make it worse.


01:05:41.050 --> 01:05:42.017
It's going to be okay.


01:05:42.717 --> 01:05:44.585
That was a very stupid
and brave thing you did.


01:05:46.221 --> 01:05:47.089
Yeah.


01:05:49.557 --> 01:05:50.458
Thank you, Wally.


01:05:58.067 --> 01:05:59.134
Hang in there, Wally.


01:06:04.273 --> 01:06:05.140
Davis.


01:06:06.942 --> 01:06:08.010
All right, stay here.


01:06:11.180 --> 01:06:13.983
Ready? One, two, three.


01:06:32.101 --> 01:06:33.269
Hey there, stranger.


01:06:33.669 --> 01:06:35.438
I didn't think you were coming
back to us.


01:06:41.444 --> 01:06:42.345
How you feeling?


01:06:44.180 --> 01:06:45.914
Good. I'm fine.


01:07:10.639 --> 01:07:11.740
Davis, can you see?


01:07:15.478 --> 01:07:16.779
Does splotchy blurs count?


01:07:19.849 --> 01:07:20.784
In this case, yes.


01:07:22.852 --> 01:07:23.787
Then no...


01:07:25.088 --> 01:07:25.989
I can't see.


01:07:34.831 --> 01:07:37.033
How else are you doing?
How's your stomach?


01:07:41.404 --> 01:07:42.639
I gotta be honest, Karen.


01:07:44.074 --> 01:07:45.275
I don't feel too good.


01:07:52.949 --> 01:07:53.917
I'll get you some water.


01:07:54.117 --> 01:07:55.151
No, no, don't... don't...
don't go! Don't...


01:07:56.086 --> 01:07:56.953
Don't go.


01:08:00.424 --> 01:08:02.058
I hate to do this to you, Karen,
but...


01:08:02.892 --> 01:08:04.562
you're just gonna have to be
stronger, all right?


01:08:05.362 --> 01:08:08.264
- Stop it.
- Get them there any way you can!


01:08:09.699 --> 01:08:10.733
Especially Ashley. She...


01:08:11.901 --> 01:08:13.304
She deserves to have a life.


01:08:14.438 --> 01:08:16.771
In a couple of days,
you're gonna feel so embarrassed


01:08:16.773 --> 01:08:18.242
about the speech you just gave.


01:08:20.777 --> 01:08:22.645
I really wish I'd met you


01:08:23.447 --> 01:08:24.948
before the end of the world.


01:08:28.885 --> 01:08:30.787
Don't do this, Davis.


01:08:31.422 --> 01:08:32.456
You know, it's funny.


01:08:35.025 --> 01:08:37.061
All these Blackhawk missions...


01:08:38.095 --> 01:08:40.264
and I get taken out
by a little mist.


01:08:43.934 --> 01:08:44.801
Davis.


01:08:53.410 --> 01:08:54.278
Davis.


01:08:59.617 --> 01:09:00.484
Davis!


01:09:38.789 --> 01:09:39.790
They've been here.


01:09:41.493 --> 01:09:42.360
Okay, relax.


01:09:42.927 --> 01:09:44.795
They're just nervous.
Wouldn't you be?


01:09:45.630 --> 01:09:46.797
Let me take care of it.


01:09:47.164 --> 01:09:48.065
Hey there.


01:09:50.734 --> 01:09:53.003
We're just looking for some
people that passed through here.


01:09:53.804 --> 01:09:55.739
Don't worry, we don't want
any trouble.


01:09:57.542 --> 01:09:59.743
Hey, hey, there's no need
for that.


01:10:00.811 --> 01:10:02.147
Maybe we can help
each other.


01:10:03.047 --> 01:10:05.517
You got something I want,
I got something you want.


01:10:06.384 --> 01:10:08.418
You tell me what happened
to the folks in that truck,


01:10:08.420 --> 01:10:09.853
and I'll serve you dinner.


01:10:10.388 --> 01:10:11.356
What?


01:10:27.539 --> 01:10:28.440
Dinner's served.


01:11:16.455 --> 01:11:17.322
Ready?


01:11:19.324 --> 01:11:20.292
Yeah.


01:11:46.985 --> 01:11:48.087
Hold. Hold on.


01:12:16.215 --> 01:12:17.149
Oh, my.


01:12:17.717 --> 01:12:18.718
Look at that!


01:12:23.022 --> 01:12:24.657
You think there's fish in there?


01:12:25.324 --> 01:12:27.694
It's a river, Wally.
A beautiful mountain river.


01:12:29.362 --> 01:12:30.329
I can hear it.


01:12:33.132 --> 01:12:33.999
Let's go.


01:12:40.841 --> 01:12:43.142
- Hey!
- Did he catch one?


01:12:43.710 --> 01:12:45.144
All right!


01:12:45.978 --> 01:12:47.647
- Hey!
- Wow!


01:12:54.654 --> 01:12:56.222
After what we've been through...


01:12:56.723 --> 01:12:59.358
it seems this is the finest meal
I've ever had.


01:13:02.596 --> 01:13:03.597
Clean water!


01:13:04.997 --> 01:13:06.265
Stars in the sky.


01:13:07.601 --> 01:13:10.404
If this is the New World Order,
count me in.


01:13:14.274 --> 01:13:15.409
I wonder if they made it.


01:13:17.210 --> 01:13:18.378
Cade probably ate them.


01:13:21.381 --> 01:13:23.583
That's not funny.


01:13:25.017 --> 01:13:25.951
He might've.


01:13:32.492 --> 01:13:33.560
I liked Vince.


01:13:35.362 --> 01:13:36.463
He wasn't such a bad guy.


01:13:38.031 --> 01:13:38.931
Crazy.


01:13:40.400 --> 01:13:41.301
But...


01:13:46.740 --> 01:13:49.609
The world was a scary place
even before all this happened.


01:13:51.244 --> 01:13:53.814
For some, it's easier
to have someone else to blame.


01:13:54.247 --> 01:13:55.148
It was "them".


01:13:56.483 --> 01:13:57.417
"They" did it.


01:14:00.220 --> 01:14:01.321
Makes it seem less random.


01:14:03.123 --> 01:14:04.859
Maybe you don't have control,
but...


01:14:06.293 --> 01:14:07.260
somebody does.


01:14:14.936 --> 01:14:15.870
Anyways,


01:14:16.336 --> 01:14:18.938
we should all probably
snuggle in and get some sleep.


01:14:18.940 --> 01:14:20.507
Tomorrow we gotta start
on the shelter.


01:14:37.090 --> 01:14:37.959
First light.


01:14:53.241 --> 01:14:55.543
- Vogel, wake up! Wake up!
- What's going on?


01:14:56.009 --> 01:14:57.343
- What's going on?
- Ashley's gone.


01:14:57.345 --> 01:14:58.312
What?


01:14:58.713 --> 01:15:00.779
I heard her scream,
and I found a jug by the river.


01:15:00.781 --> 01:15:02.314
Oh, my God, what if
she fell in the river?


01:15:02.316 --> 01:15:03.651
That's not all I found.


01:15:06.052 --> 01:15:06.888
Cade.


01:15:07.555 --> 01:15:08.856
He left it where I'd see it.


01:15:09.891 --> 01:15:11.657
But I think if Ashley
hadn't screamed,


01:15:11.659 --> 01:15:12.927
he would've
killed us all in our sleep.


01:15:16.664 --> 01:15:18.864
- I'll get the others.
- Listen to me very carefully.


01:15:18.866 --> 01:15:21.001
Get them and head up river
as far as you can


01:15:21.003 --> 01:15:22.868
and don't stop
until you find someplace


01:15:22.870 --> 01:15:24.303
- with some cover.
- No.


01:15:24.305 --> 01:15:25.506
I'll catch up to you if I can.


01:15:27.041 --> 01:15:29.141
The last thing Davis asked me
was to make sure that


01:15:29.143 --> 01:15:31.710
Ashley got a chance
at life, and I'm gonna do that.


01:15:31.712 --> 01:15:33.648
- Karen...
- I'm not losing anyone else.


01:15:35.616 --> 01:15:37.585
I think all this survival
stuff's gone to your head.


01:15:38.286 --> 01:15:39.821
How are you gonna handle Cade,
huh?


01:15:45.626 --> 01:15:48.329
I may not be a survivalist,
but at least I'm prepared.


01:15:52.801 --> 01:15:55.403
Get them to safety, Larry Vogel.
I'm counting on you.


01:16:29.538 --> 01:16:31.974
I was really hoping you'd be
bringing that bottle with you.


01:16:33.542 --> 01:16:34.509
My new friends


01:16:35.176 --> 01:16:36.778
weren't happy
about having me give it up.


01:16:38.447 --> 01:16:39.314
You okay?


01:16:39.881 --> 01:16:40.782
Don't worry about her.


01:16:41.883 --> 01:16:42.951
She's just fine.


01:16:44.252 --> 01:16:45.253
Let her go, Cade.


01:16:50.192 --> 01:16:51.326
This sweet little lamb?


01:16:52.961 --> 01:16:54.429
I don't think I could bear
doing that.


01:16:57.766 --> 01:16:58.667
She's just...


01:16:59.468 --> 01:17:00.502
cute enough to eat.


01:17:03.472 --> 01:17:05.173
So, why don't you put
that scattergun down?


01:17:06.109 --> 01:17:07.643
'Cause you're making
those boys twitchy.


01:17:19.588 --> 01:17:20.555
Come to me, Ashley.


01:17:21.323 --> 01:17:22.959
- Come on over here. We...
- Don't.


01:17:25.627 --> 01:17:27.329
This isn't something
you can win, Karen.


01:17:27.830 --> 01:17:29.164
It's not a negotiation.


01:17:30.465 --> 01:17:31.666
There's nothing you can offer me


01:17:31.668 --> 01:17:33.201
that I couldn't just take
from you.


01:17:34.637 --> 01:17:36.105
And what is it that you want,
Cade?


01:17:39.976 --> 01:17:41.176
I want my radio back.


01:17:43.913 --> 01:17:46.747
You know, if it wasn't for you,
I'd be safe and sound


01:17:46.749 --> 01:17:48.551
with all the comforts
at home right now.


01:17:50.486 --> 01:17:52.753
If it wasn't for me,
you'd be dead


01:17:52.755 --> 01:17:55.725
in a hole in the ground
where Pleasant Creek used to be!


01:17:57.026 --> 01:17:58.127
Don't bet on it.


01:17:59.796 --> 01:18:02.262
I'll tell you one thing,
I wouldn't be out here


01:18:02.264 --> 01:18:04.867
in the middle of nowhere
with nothing to eat!


01:18:05.233 --> 01:18:07.570
If you're mad at me,
take it out on me!


01:18:08.404 --> 01:18:09.439
Let the girl go!


01:18:12.341 --> 01:18:13.443
It's not gonna happen.


01:18:16.479 --> 01:18:17.880
You took everything from me.


01:18:19.015 --> 01:18:20.581
And now I'm taking everything
from you,


01:18:20.583 --> 01:18:22.186
and I do mean everything.


01:18:22.885 --> 01:18:24.188
You know you were wrong, Cade.


01:18:26.723 --> 01:18:28.190
Wrong about what, Karen?


01:18:28.192 --> 01:18:30.092
Being a leader
isn't about who's willing


01:18:30.094 --> 01:18:32.795
to take it the furthest
or choosing the right path.


01:18:34.263 --> 01:18:38.202
It's about how far is too far,
and knowing when to stop.


01:18:40.536 --> 01:18:43.339
I'll write that in the marker
we leave over your bones...


01:18:45.308 --> 01:18:46.944
after we lick them clean.


01:18:56.285 --> 01:18:57.121
Damn.


01:18:58.088 --> 01:18:58.956
You were right.


01:19:07.630 --> 01:19:08.598
Come on.


01:19:22.880 --> 01:19:24.782
- Come here, baby girl.
- I'm not a baby!


01:19:25.616 --> 01:19:26.784
Damn little mongrel!


01:19:28.786 --> 01:19:30.587
Hey! Hey!


01:19:58.649 --> 01:19:59.516
Karen!


01:20:02.253 --> 01:20:03.154
Karen.


01:20:06.089 --> 01:20:06.957
Karen.


01:20:07.825 --> 01:20:08.692
Hey!


01:20:25.210 --> 01:20:26.211
Hey.


01:21:01.713 --> 01:21:02.680
Oh, thank God!


01:21:04.148 --> 01:21:05.984
We didn't think
that they'd find you.


01:21:07.051 --> 01:21:08.553
They wouldn't let us go along.


01:21:12.590 --> 01:21:13.524
What is this?


01:21:14.092 --> 01:21:15.593
A military base?
How did you find them?


01:21:16.527 --> 01:21:18.796
- They found us.
- Come here, Ashley.


01:21:20.031 --> 01:21:22.066
Come on, let this nice lady take
a look at you.


01:21:22.934 --> 01:21:24.334
You can sit
next to Mayor Wally.


01:21:24.336 --> 01:21:25.270
Sit right here.


01:21:28.340 --> 01:21:31.442
It's okay. They have to check us
out before they let us in.


01:21:31.743 --> 01:21:33.544
In where? Who are "they"?


01:21:40.051 --> 01:21:41.253
They won't really say.


01:21:43.322 --> 01:21:44.687
<i>Attention.</i>


01:21:44.689 --> 01:21:47.393
<i>Lockdown in two minutes.</i>


01:21:49.228 --> 01:21:50.129
But it's "them".


01:21:51.363 --> 01:21:52.430
Just like Vince said.


01:21:53.698 --> 01:21:55.034
A New World Order.


01:21:56.268 --> 01:21:58.937
They've a bunker
that goes down 20 stories.


01:22:01.606 --> 01:22:04.243
I don't care who they are,
as long as we're safe.


01:22:05.110 --> 01:22:07.279
I could use some rule of law,
about now.


01:22:08.414 --> 01:22:10.581
So, we trade our freedom
for security?


01:22:11.449 --> 01:22:12.952
Cade was right about one thing.


01:22:14.119 --> 01:22:15.453
You're a conspiracy nut.


01:22:31.003 --> 01:22:32.871
What was that acronym
Cade used to use?


01:22:33.739 --> 01:22:36.675
- Teo-toky or something?
- Teotwawki.


01:22:37.977 --> 01:22:39.678
The end of the world
as we know it.


01:22:43.115 --> 01:22:44.783
I'm not sure
what to believe anymore.


01:22:45.617 --> 01:22:49.254
It's gonna be a long winter.


01:22:50.956 --> 01:22:54.994
<i>Lockdown happening, one minute.</i>


01:23:04.257 --> 01:23:09.257
Subtitles by explosiveskull

